#AI:1
TYPE="path_rules"
GLOB="**/*.go"

LANGUAGE_RUNTIME:
- Go 1.22+ (fill in exact version in go.mod)
- go modules — no GOPATH-style dependency management

BUILD:
- go build ./...
- go vet ./...
- golangci-lint run

STYLE_CONVENTIONS:
- gofmt is law — never hand-format
- goimports for import grouping (stdlib / external / internal)
- Exported names get godoc comments; unexported names rarely need comments
- Error wrapping: fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err) — always wrap with context
- Accept interfaces, return structs (at package boundary)

FORBIDDEN_PATTERNS:
- No panic() in library code — return errors
- No init() functions except in main packages — initialization order is a footgun
- No global mutable state outside of main
- No log.Fatal() outside of main — callers should decide how to handle errors

EXPLICITLY_NOT_TOUCHING:
- (fill in: generated protobuf/grpc code, vendor/ directory, etc.)
